// Title: Potential Binary Proxy Execution Via Cdb.EXE
// Sigma ID: b5c7395f-e501-4a08-94d4-57fe7a9da9d2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Beyu Denis, oscd.community, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-26 | Modified: 2024-04-22
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1106, T1218, T1127
// Description: Detects usage of "cdb.exe" to launch arbitrary processes or commands from a debugger script file
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of debugging tools
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Cdb/
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20170715043507/http://www.exploit-monday.com/2016/08/windbg-cdb-shellcode-runner.html
//   - https://twitter.com/nas_bench/status/1534957360032120833
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cdb_arbitrary_command_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cdb.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CDB.Exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -cf ")
